# This repository's own commit scopes, one per line. Blank lines and # comments
# are ignored.
#
# `workbench commits check` accepts Workbench's built-in process scopes (agents,
# ci, decision, deps, docs, guides, policy, release, rules, skills, templates,
# treewide, vision) and the name of any real proposal file —
# `proposals/<NNNN>-<slug>.md` is the scope `<NNNN>-<slug>` — without an entry
# here. List only the scopes for parts of this repository the process does not
# name. Prefer the narrowest scope that accurately describes the change.
#
# `proposal` is listed because proposals are a feature of Workbench. Work on one
# proposal takes that proposal's `<NNNN>-<slug>`.

cli
hooks
proposal
readme
site
tools
